```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
2result.sql divides the count of “None checked” births by the true total‑births for each county by joining to the county_natality table, so the percentage of births without maternal morbidity is accurate. It also pads county FIPS codes (LPAD) to ensure the join with ACS geo_id is correct. 1result.sql omits both of these safeguards—its denominator is the sum of all morbidity‑category rows (which double‑counts births) and it does not pad FIPS—so its correlation values are biased.